{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Player Goal.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Player Goal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"player goal player goal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Player Goal.md","fileName":"Player Goal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Player Goal","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Player Experience Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Player Experience Design","Feedback","Core Gameplay Loop","Progression System","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Player Goal.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Player Goal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"player goal player goal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Player Goal.md","fileName":"Player Goal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Player Goal","heading":"Player Goal","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A player goal is a desired state that organizes attention and action during play. Goals can operate over immediate, short-term, and long-term timescales and may be supplied explicitly by the game or created by the player.\n\nGoals give consequences meaning and allow [[Feedback]] to be interpreted as progress, setback, or new opportunity. Nested goals connect moment-to-moment [[Core Gameplay Loop|core loops]] to broader [[Progression System|progression]].\n\nA goal may be explicit, implied by the system's rewards and resistance, selected from many authored objectives, or invented by the player inside an open system. Increasing player control over purpose widens the conversation but does not remove the boundaries established by the rules.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Player Experience Design","Feedback","Core Gameplay Loop","Progression System","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Player Goal.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Player Goal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"player goal player goal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Player Goal.md","fileName":"Player Goal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Player Goal","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n[[agamedesignvocabulary.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Player Experience Design","Feedback","Core Gameplay Loop","Progression System","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}